  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "chi(X) = C_W[ prod_{i=1..9} X_i ], X in [0,1]^9. C_W is a wrapper/normalizer, NOT a tenth multiplicand inside the product; currently the identity map on [0,1] pending explicit definition; map_zero C_W(0) = 0 preserves the veto through the wrapper. Lean proves the wrapper structure (chi_zero_if_any_factor_zero; wrapper adds no tenth multiplicand) - it does not prove the wrapper is Christ; that identification is a bridge claim. The chi = C identity is what the framework converges on if all nine mappings hold: nine independent equations, same structure, same asymmetry position, same functional form - the convergence is the argument. Open at source: C_W boundary behavior (AM-5 closure conditions), identity-map ratification, and the spacetime-integral form (DEFERRED, not canon).",
  "statementPlain": "Multiply the nine laws together and wrap the product - that wrapped value is coherence. The wrapper math is machine-proved: zero in any factor kills the whole, and the wrapper adds no secret tenth term. The claim that this wrapped coherence IS Christ is a separate claim - asserted by convergence of the nine, not proven - and it stands or falls with them: break one law and the integral changes; break all nine and the framework falls. Its own kill condition is named: if the asymmetry terms do not cancel at full integration, the identity fails.",
  "mathematicalForm": "chi(X) = C_W[ prod_{i=1..9} X_i ]; C_W(0) = 0; C_W currently identity on [0,1]; chi = C iff all nine mappings hold (convergence claim)",
  "mathFormNormal": "chi(X) = C_W[ prod_{i=1..9} X_i ]; C_W(0) = 0; C_W currently identity on [0,1]; chi = C iff all nine mappings hold (convergence claim)",
